multiple-choice questions for https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B

    llm.decide(state, "did the deployment succeed?", ["yes", "no", "unclear"])
    -> {"yes": 0.91, "no": 0.03, "unclear": 0.06}

a chat model answers by generating tokens, one forward pass each,
and then you parse the text. but the very first forward pass
already contains the answer: the logits for A, B and C. this repo
reads those and stops. one pass, no generation, no parsing, and a
probability for every option instead of one sampled string.

ask 21 questions about the same document and the document is
prefilled once, the 21 questions run as one batch.

the catch: the model cannot think before it answers. this is its
gut reaction. for hard decisions or free-form output, use chat.

https://github.com/TheoLeeCJ/openjev did this with a 4B model.

quick demo:

    $ ./run.sh uv run example.py
